# --- Forward captured leads to a Google Sheet ---
# Required: the spreadsheet ID (the long token from the sheet URL,
# docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<ID>/...). The first row of "Sheet1" will be
# filled in automatically with column headers the first time a row is appended.
# GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=1IV1O73AKZrWl4Io1qVAO5zBBQD5c7UXBPfE2XU92YgU
#
# Auth: choose ONE of the following two paths.
#
# (A) Service account (recommended, portable across hosts including Hetzner):
#     create a Google Cloud service account, enable the Google Sheets API, share
#     the sheet with the service account email as Editor, then store the entire
#     downloaded JSON key file as the value of this single env var.
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON={"type":"service_account",...}
#
# (B) Replit `google-sheet` OAuth integration: connect the integration from the
#     Replit sidebar. Only works inside a Replit container. Used automatically
#     when GOOGLE_SHEETS_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON is not set.
